# Where your photo library is. Template -- copy it, do not edit it in place:
#
#     cp _datapath .datapath
#
# then edit `.datapath` to point at your own data. `.datapath` is gitignored, so
# your local path never dirties the tree and is never committed by accident.
# This file is the tracked template and should keep pointing at ./sample_data,
# so a fresh clone that ignores all of this still runs.
#
# Format: one path, on a line of its own. Blank lines and `#` comments are
# ignored, and the first path that survives that wins. Relative paths are taken
# from the repository root, not from your shell's working directory, so a run
# started anywhere resolves the same. `~` is expanded.
#
# Whatever you point at must contain a `jpg/` directory -- that is the test, and
# it is the same test for every candidate. The usual shape:
#
#     <your path>/jpg/<library>/<trip>/*.jpg
#     <your path>/xmp/<library>/<trip>/*.xmp      # optional; not every JPEG has one
#     <your path>/label/                          # produced by a labelling run
#
# You do not need this file at all if you are using either default: the private
# `data/` submodule if you have access to it, or the shipped sample otherwise.
# It exists for a library that lives somewhere else entirely.
#
# Examples:
#     /mnt/photos/library
#     ~/Pictures/birds
#     ../my-photo-export

./sample_data
